&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step into a career with ASM, where cutting edge technology meets collaborative culture. &lt;/strong&gt;​&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For over 55 years ASM has been ahead of what’s next, at the forefront of innovation and what’s technologically possible. With more than 4,500 ASMers representing 70 nationalities, our people and our advanced semiconductor devices are playing a crucial role in trends such as 5G, cloud computing, AI, and autonomous driving.  But&amp;nbsp;we’re more than just a tech company. We value diversity, inclusion and sustainability as we strive to make a positive impact on the world.&amp;nbsp; Our development programs help support your growth, shaping your future and pushing the boundaries of innovation to unleash potential.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;ASM is a leading global provider of products, services, and materials for semiconductor processing. Innovation has been at the heart of everything we do for over half a century. The brilliant minds at ASM are dedicated to developing groundbreaking solutions for the world&#39;s leading semiconductor manufacturers. Every day, we drive the development of next-generation computer chip technologies, staying a few steps ahead of the future. Our talented and enthusiastic employees are just like you: committed to improving people&#39;s lives and unlocking new possibilities. Through a collaborative approach to research and development, we advance key semiconductor technologies and platforms such as ALD, epitaxy, PEALD, PECVD, and vertical furnaces. We have also recently entered the promising growth market of silicon carbide epitaxy. Year after year, our innovations help make chips smaller, faster, and more powerful. In fact, you can find our technology in every aspect of modern life: in artificial intelligence, medical devices, 5G, smartphones, autonomous driving, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performing installations, implementing new developments, and conducting qualification procedures, as well as carrying out preventive and corrective maintenance on complex electronic/electromechanical semiconductor equipment at ASM customer sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performing repairs during equipment downtime, collaborating in diverse teams, and developing and presenting proposed solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working on-site at various customer locations within cleanroom environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Willingness to travel: Within the ASM Europe region, we have many customers spread across the entire area. Therefore, a willingness to travel for business—both within Germany and to other European countries—is a requirement. Due to ASM’s growing international presence and expanding customer base, occasional business trips to North America or Asia may also be necessary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Profile:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Mechatronics, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or Electronics (or equivalent knowledge); applications from certified master craftsmen and technicians are also welcome&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using measuring instruments and hand tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills (German and English)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in MS Office; SAP knowledge is an advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ideal candidate brings initial professional experience in field service or customer support and has gained experience in the assembly and commissioning of systems, preferably within the semiconductor industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We also welcome applications from suitable entry-level candidates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Class B driver’s license mandatory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer at ASM:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to work for a leading provider of semiconductor process equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A varied and dynamic international environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An attractive salary package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company car for business and private use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At ASM, we are committed to supporting our employees and empowering them to develop their talents and perform at their best. We actively foster an inclusive and diverse culture built on trust and transparency. Our people are our strength, and we value the differences each individual brings, as they make us a better team. By embracing a wide range of perspectives, we cultivate a culture of continuous exploration and the adoption of new ideas. At every step, we recognize that it is our valued employees who enable us to deliver outstanding products and services to our customers—and to make a positive impact on society.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us on our journey. Discover how you can be part of our exciting future and apply today! To learn more about ASM, visit us at asm.com and on LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, and YouTube.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply today to be part of what’s next.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We make the tech that enables the chips in devices which improve lives around the world. We do this with an eye to the future, pushing the boundaries of what’s possible through cutting-edge innovation, and driving the next wave of technological breakthroughs that shape how we live, work, and connect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;To learn more about ASM, find us at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.asm.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;asm.com&lt;/a&gt; and&amp;nbsp;on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/asm/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/ASMOfficialCompany&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/asmofficialcompany/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Instagram,&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/ASMofficialco&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;X&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/c/ASM_Official&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;ASM is an equal opportunity employer and considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, age, nationality, social or ethnic origin, sexual orientation, gender, gender identify or expression, marital status, pregnancy, political affiliation, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Residency in Germany is required. This role is currently fully remote&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At JFrog, we’re reinventing DevOps to help the world’s greatest companies innovate -- and we want you along for the ride. This is a special place with a unique combination of brilliance, spirit and just all-around great people. Here, if you’re willing to do more, your career can take off. And since software plays a central role in everyone’s lives, you’ll be part of an important mission. Thousands of customers, including the majority of the Fortune 100, trust JFrog to manage, accelerate, and secure their software delivery from code to production -- a concept we call “liquid software.” Wouldn&#39;t it be amazing if you could join us in our journey?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Solution Architect &lt;/strong&gt;to be on the front lines, working closely with our customers and prospects, guiding them on how to build robust DevSecOps processes. You will work with our sales, product, customer success &amp;amp; engineering teams to help customers understand the value of JFrog Solution from a technical and business perspective.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you love working with brilliant people, being part of an energetic team and changing the world of software, you might be the perfect Frog to join our team!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Solution Architect, New Logo in JFrog you will...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner and Collaborate with account executives to understand customer requirements and propose customized technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business objectives into technical requirements and solution designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct discovery sessions, technical presentations, and product demonstrations for prospective customers in both English and German.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct compelling Proof of Values (POVs), and product demonstrations to showcase the value and impact of JFrog solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support transition from pre-sales to post-sales, ensuring continuity and alignment of expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to RFPs, RFIs, and technical questionnaires, including those in German-speaking markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent JFrog at industry events and conferences, highlighting the transformative potential of JFrog products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence JFrog’s product roadmap by communicating customer feedback and identifying trends in the DevOps and DevSecOps landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay ahead of industry trends, continuously enhancing your knowledge of emerging technologies in DevOps, cloud infrastructure, and software development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be a Solution Architect, New Logo in JFrog you need...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7-10+ years of experience in technical sales, presales, or sales engineering roles (experience with MEDDPICC is a plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven expertise in DevOps tools and methodologies, including Docker, Kubernetes, CI servers, Git, Artifactory, and build tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience building software pipelines using diverse DevOps tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on experience&lt;/strong&gt; with Linux and cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, or GCP) – mandatory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with software architecture design, scalable product development, and on-premise/cloud hybrid environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering POVs and technical demonstrations to diverse stakeholders, from technical teams to business leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A customer-centric mindset with a &quot;can-do&quot; attitude and a passion for learning and solving complex problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and presentation skills, capable of translating technical concepts into business value for varied audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;As an iOS Engineer on the Design System team, you&#39;ll translate SumUp&#39;s design language into a reusable, easy-to-use library of UI components and experience patterns — empowering product teams to build cohesive, accessible user experiences at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Design System team works hand-in-hand with the Mobile Platform team to set standards and provide guidance across all product teams at SumUp. As we expand our ecosystem of merchant and consumer-facing products, this role offers a rare opportunity to shape the foundation that helps developers build faster and ship higher-quality experiences to millions of users worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the core experience for both users and developers interacting with SumUp&#39;s iOS ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with product and design teams to build components that are maintainable, consistent, and beautiful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed accessibility best practices into every component — from content descriptions and touch target sizing to color contrast and dynamic type&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on technical guidance to product teams to deliver on company priorities, including the upcoming support for landscape orientation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review code contributions, enforce design system conventions, and mentor engineers on best practices for reusable UI development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the migration of legacy UIKit-based components to SwiftUI while maintaining system stability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify and address technical debt to uphold a high bar for engineering excellence and codebase health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll be a great fit for this role if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring 3+ years of professional iOS development experience, ideally on large-scale or consumer-facing applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are fluent in Swift, with deep hands-on knowledge of both SwiftUI and UIKit — and a clear view on when and how to use each&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring experience building or contributing to a design system, component library, or shared UI framework, and understand what it takes to make components truly reusable and scalable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take pride in crafting accessible user experiences — you know your way around VoiceOver, dynamic type, color contrast, and touch target standards, and treat accessibility as a first-class concern, not an afterthought&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a strong grasp of testing best practices for UI components, including unit tests, snapshot tests, and UI automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable reviewing code and mentoring peers — you enjoy sharing knowledge, giving constructive feedback, and raising the bar for the whole team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are self-motivated and structured in your working style — you manage your own priorities, communicate clearly in English, and thrive in a cross-functional, collaborative environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay genuinely curious about the iOS ecosystem — you follow Apple&#39;s releases closely, experiment with new APIs, and are excited to bring fresh ideas back to the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you should join SumUp:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 Opportunity to work with SumUppers globally on large-scale fintech products used by millions of businesses worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌈 Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion: be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone&#39;s perspectives are respected and embraced.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚀 Enrolment onto our Virtual Stock Option programme: you will own a stake in SumUp’s future success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚 A dedicated annual L&amp;amp;D budget for your individual development, which can be used to attend conferences and/or advancing your career through further education.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💶 Competitive Health &amp;amp; Life Insurance: Includes comprehensive cover (optical, dental) and Life Assurance (2 x your salary).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰 Financial Future: A corporate pension scheme and a referral bonus for bringing in top talent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏖️ Generous time off: 28 days of paid leave plus public holidays and special leave days.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌴 Break4me: 1-month paid sabbatical after 3 years of service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎉 Culture of Connection: Attend global offsites and/or hackathons with your teammates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About SumUp&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in the everyday hero.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Small business owners are at the heart of all we do, so we&#39;re creating tools that help them run their businesses. With a founder’s mentality and a &#39;team-first’ attitude, our diverse teams across Europe, South America and the United States work together to ensure that the small business owners we partner with can be successful doing what they love.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SumUp is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that proudly pursues and hires a diverse workforce. SumUp does not make hiring or employment decisions on the basis of race, colour, religion or religious belief, ethnic or national origin, nationality, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, age or any other basis protected by applicable laws or prohibited by company policy. SumUp also strives for a healthy and safe workplace and strictly prohibits harassment of any kind.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SumUp will not accept unsolicited resumes from any source other than directly from a candidate&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Application Tip&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We recognise that candidates feel they need to meet 100% of the job criteria in order to apply for a job. Please note that this is only a guide. If you don’t tick every box, it’s ok too because it means you have room to learn and develop your career at SumUp.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Please note that we will never request payment or bank account information at any stage of the recruitment process. As we continue to grow our teams, we urge you to be cautious of fraudulent job postings or recruitment activities that misuse our company name and information. Please protect your personal information during any recruitment process. While Monks may contact potential candidates via LinkedIn, all applications must be submitted through our official website (&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--focus-visible&quot; href=&quot;http://monks.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://monks.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;monks.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Security Operations Analyst to serve as our primary operational anchor for EMEA, bridging follow-the-sun operations across global time zones (APAC and the Americas). In this role, you will analyse security events, investigate potential threats, validate and manage high-priority incidents, and execute decisive containment actions to minimise overall impact while escalating unresolved incidents to security engineering teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This person will monitor and remediate security incidents across on-prem, identity, and cloud-based environments for internal corporate infrastructure and enterprise client engagements. As the primary responder on shift during EMEA business hours, you should possess deep operational muscle memory, strong technical composure under pressure, and the initiative to challenge assumptions and propose continuous improvements. This is a remote role from either the UK, Ireland, or Poland.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead triage, scoping, containment, and eradication for medium-to-high severity security incidents across endpoint, identity, SaaS, and cloud environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform deep-dive investigations, threat isolation, and query hunting leveraging CrowdStrike Falcon (Host Timeline, Real Time Response).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate identity compromises, phishing campaigns, and suspicious account activities using Google Admin Console (Investigation Tool, Email Log Search, Token Auditing).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse ingress edge telemetry, CDN traffic patterns, WAF events, and web server logs (including Cloudflare and Acquia application environments) to detect, trace, and mitigate web attacks, DDoS conditions, and botnet/scraping abuse.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and continuously update incident response plans and runbooks for efficient incident response, collaborating with engineering to automate containment workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate cross-departmental remediation tasks and escalate unresolved incidents with clear technical root-cause analysis (RCA) aligned with MITRE ATT&amp;amp;CK.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with content production for security awareness and mentorship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The essentials:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of direct experience in Security Operations (SOC), Incident Response, or similar hands-on technical operational roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science/Engineering/Information Security, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep operational experience utilising CrowdStrike (investigation workflows, Host Timeline, Real Time Response, and query hunting).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leveraging Google Admin Console (Investigation Tool, Email Log Search, Token Auditing) for phishing, BEC, and identity investigations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with industry-leading security tools across EDR, SWG, SIEM, and MDM platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of network protocols, traffic flow, and the OSI model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with log analysis, malware triage, and digital forensics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of operating autonomously during incidents with minimal supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience leveraging AI tools, LLMs, or agentic workflows to assist analysis, scripting, or automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working ITIL knowledge and functional familiarity with the MITRE ATT&amp;amp;CK framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Courteous, articulate, and educated in interpersonal delivery. Maintains a polite, respectful, and calm demeanor with internal teammates, leadership, and external clients even during incident bridges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to confidently and politely present findings to technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-directed, resourceful, and critical thinker with proactive problem-solving instincts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong personal anxiety management and self-organisation during high-pressure incidents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eager to learn, experiment with emerging tooling, and actively suggest process enhancements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Not a must, but a plus:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated hands-on and reflexive triage/containment instincts over theoretical knowledge or paper certifications (certifications like CISSP, Sec+, or CEH are welcome, but secondary to proven live-fire execution).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience analysing Cloudflare edge/WAF logs and Acquia/Drupal web server access logs for application-layer anomalies, scraping, and volumetric spikes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with modern SIEM / SecOps platforms:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud security experience (GCP, AWS, Azure) in production environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scripting proficiency (Python, PowerShell, Bash) for automated triage and API data collection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to Blue/Red/Purple team simulation exercises.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;#LI-RE1 #LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Monks &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Monks is the global, digital-first, data-driven, unitary operating brand of S4Capital plc, where our culture centers on how we show up for the work and for one another. That begins with the commitment to strive for mastery—taking deep pride in our craft and creating work that sets the bar. In everyday execution, we drive momentum by choosing bold action rather than waiting for certainty. Above all, our teams are stronger together, bringing diverse perspectives into a unified team that communicates with clarity, trust, and mutual respect.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;This commitment to craft and innovation translates directly into widespread industry acclaim: Monks was named a Contender in The Forrester Wave™: Global Marketing Services and a leader in the 2026 Gartner® Magic Quadrant™ for Global Digital Marketing Agencies. It ranks among Cannes Lions&#39; Top 10 Creative Companies (2022-25) and remains the only partner featured in AdExchanger’s Programmatic Power Players list every year (2020-24). Named Adweek’s first AI Agency of the Year (2023) and The One Show’s inaugural AI Pioneer Organization (2025), Monks was also awarded Business Intelligence Group’s 2026 Excellence in Artificial Intelligence Award in the Human-Machine Interaction Team category. Additionally, Monks.Flow earned AI-based Marketing Solution of the Year at the 2026 AI Breakthrough Awards and a 2026 Global Generative AI Award in the Agentic Marketing Innovation category. Finally, Monks achieved a record-breaking number of FWAs and continues to hold the most of any partner.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;We are an equal-opportunity employer committed to building a respectful and empowering work environment for all people to freely express themselves amongst colleagues who embrace diversity in all respects. Including fresh voices and unique points of view in all aspects of our business not only creates an environment where we can all grow and thrive but also increases our potential to produce work that better represents—and resonates with—the world around us.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;iframe src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/bY0nNPT75xY&quot; width=&quot;560&quot; height=&quot;314&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer | Autoplanner | Hybrid Working | London&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Introduction:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are Ocado Group, and we&#39;re bringing world-class automation to online grocery. Our Ocado Smart Platform (OSP) combines cutting-edge robotics, AI, and IoT within our advanced CFCs (Customer Fulfilment Centres). We&#39;ve mastered the single pick, transforming online delivery for our global partners. Join us and be part of a team pushing the boundaries of retail technology.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Software Engineer in the Autoplanner team, you will own the software engineering that brings our data science and machine learning products into live production. Autoplanner builds AI-powered systems that unify planning across global warehouses and last-mile assets, delivering globally optimized plans that maximize profit and minimize lateness. You will act as the engineering partner to our data scientists, ensuring our systems remain robust, highly scalable, and efficient as we roll out to more international retail partners. Our services are mostly Python, but we use Java where a service integrates closely with the Ocado Smart Platform, to take advantage of its shared tooling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will write typed, well-tested Python and oversee cloud-based data applications from end to end. You will contribute to core architectural decisions, improve CI/CD pipelines, and raise engineering standards across the team through pairing, code reviews, and shared tooling. Additionally, you will harness AI coding tools in production while maintaining a strong emphasis on engineering discipline, system performance, and high-quality software craft.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain data- and ML-driven, cloud-based applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain robust APIs and data contracts for data science teams and broader Ocado systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage cloud deployments and continuously improve CI/CD pipelines across diverse AWS environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Package, version, serve, and monitor machine learning models in live production environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive architecture decisions across repository, application, and system levels, documenting them as Architecture Decision Records (ADRs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with data scientists to transition advanced algorithms and models into scalable production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with software engineers across Ocado Technology to integrate applications within the Ocado Smart Platform (OSP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Elevate engineering practices across the team through pairing, code reviews, shared tooling, and responsible AI agent integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share in on-call and production support responsibilities for critical live operational services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience as a Senior Software Engineer owning end-to-end production Python services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive background building data-intensive cloud applications, preferably asynchronous, event-driven, or queue-based architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong practical knowledge of AWS and/or GCP identity, networking, and messaging services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid software design capabilities, including defining system boundaries and crafting high-level architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rigorous testing and delivery discipline, encompassing integration testing and modern CI/CD practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on MLOps experience, specifically in packaging, serving, and monitoring ML models in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record of collaborating effectively with data scientists and cross-functional engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience using AI coding agents on production codebases, with a sharp judgment on validating and verifying AI-generated output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in supporting our people with meaningful, flexible benefits that prioritise well-being and work-life balance. Here’s a snapshot of what you can expect:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Time to recharge:&lt;/strong&gt; 25 days annual leave (rising to 27 after 5 years), plus the option to buy more – and 30 days a year to work from anywhere in the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health &amp;amp; wellbeing:&lt;/strong&gt; Private Medical Insurance from your first month, wellbeing support through specialist apps and EAP, plus Income Protection and Life Assurance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Family-first policies:&lt;/strong&gt; 22 weeks paid maternity/primary carer leave and 6 weeks paid paternity leave.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial support:&lt;/strong&gt; Pension with employer matching up to 7%, share schemes (Sharesave &amp;amp; BAYE), and interest-free loans for train tickets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commuter perks:&lt;/strong&gt; Cycle to Work Scheme and free shuttle buses to/from Hatfield and Welwyn Garden City stations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exclusive discounts:&lt;/strong&gt; 15% off at Ocado.com with free delivery (starting in your first month).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be bold, be unique, be brilliant, be you. We are looking for individuality and we value diversity. We are an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to treating all applicants and employees fairly and equally. We are committed to making reasonable adjustments to provide a positive, barrier-free recruitment process and supportive work environment. If you have any support or access requirements, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-HYBRID&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-JT1&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;iframe src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/bY0nNPT75xY&quot; width=&quot;560&quot; height=&quot;314&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Scientist | Autoplanner | Hybrid Working | London&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Introduction:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are Ocado Group, and we&#39;re bringing world-class automation to online grocery. Our Ocado Smart Platform (OSP) combines cutting-edge robotics, AI, and IoT within our advanced CFCs (Customer Fulfilment Centres). We&#39;ve mastered the single pick, transforming online delivery for our global partners. Join us and be part of a team pushing the boundaries of retail technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Data Scientist within our Autoplanner team, you will build AI-powered systems that unify planning across global warehouses and last-mile operations. You will be responsible for developing the machine learning models, optimisation algorithms, and operational simulations that underpin our core planning products. By taking high-impact models from concept through to monitored production systems, you will ensure automated operational plans are robust, globally optimised, and trusted to run live across our partners&#39; international supply chains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working closely with cross-functional software engineers and product managers, you will set the technical direction for key initiatives while mentoring colleagues to elevate the team’s overall data science capabilities. You will also engage directly with internal and external stakeholders, including global retail partners - to translate complex logistics challenges into production-ready data science solutions, shaping the future of autonomous operational planning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver machine learning models for planning products, iterating from initial prototype to evaluated and monitored production artefacts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore innovative modelling and optimisation approaches, benchmarking and testing them rigorously against existing solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and extend simulations of warehouse operations and customer demand to validate and power live operational plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and measure business-critical metrics using robust statistical techniques, establishing the team&#39;s standards for model evaluation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the technical direction and delivery strategy for the data science initiatives you lead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the technical capabilities of data scientists across the team through mentoring, technical guidance, and collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with software engineers to ensure models are cleanly packaged, deployed, monitored, and efficiently served on the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own relationships with product managers, internal partner teams, and external retailers to align on requirements and delivery roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Essential&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of taking data science and machine learning models into production, maintaining them, and leading initiatives end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong machine learning and statistical expertise, including the ability to evaluate model performance rigorously against business metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in writing production-quality Python code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience querying and working with large datasets in cloud data warehouses such as BigQuery, including implementing data-quality checks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building simulations or stochastic models of operational systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience using AI coding agents, alongside the critical judgement to verify and test generated code and outputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with software engineers, product managers, and diverse business stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Nice to Haves&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mathematical optimisation frameworks and toolkits, such as OR-Tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with discrete-event simulation libraries, such as SimPy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background or domain knowledge in logistics, supply chain, or operational research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in supporting our people with meaningful, flexible benefits that prioritise well-being and work-life balance. Here’s a snapshot of what you can expect:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time to recharge: 25 days annual leave (rising to 27 after 5 years), plus the option to buy more – and 30 days a year to work from anywhere in the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health &amp;amp; wellbeing: Private Medical Insurance from your first month, wellbeing support through specialist apps and EAP, plus Income Protection and Life Assurance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-first policies: 22 weeks paid maternity/primary carer leave and 6 weeks paid paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial support: Pension with employer matching up to 7%, share schemes (Sharesave &amp;amp; BAYE), and interest-free loans for train tickets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commuter perks: Cycle to Work Scheme and free shuttle buses to/from Hatfield and Welwyn Garden City stations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exclusive discounts: 15% off at Ocado.com with free delivery (starting in your first month).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be bold, be unique, be brilliant, be you. We are looking for individuality and we value diversity. We are an equal opportunities employer and we are committed to treating all applicants and employees fairly and equally. We are committed to making reasonable adjustments to provide a positive, barrier-free recruitment process and supportive work environment. If you have any support or access requirements, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application.&lt;/p&gt;
